  "reviewMatrix": {
    "architecture": "Reuses authenticated purchase-order route, shell, organization context, module entitlement service and existing envelope/proposal/event records. Shared route helper adds an optional presentation callback; guard behavior is unchanged.",
    "backend_api": "Strict bounded commands reject client authority and bind the current order/proposal revisions. Action adapters derive buyer/tenant/session; transaction-owned checks run again. Exact invitation/review/revocation identities are distinct from similar outcomes.",
    "database_migrations": "Serializable transactions and current actor/session/role/grant locks protect scoped effects. Audit failure rolls back; concurrent duplicate requests converge through exact retry. Existing append-only records remain. No schema migration.",
    "security_iam_privacy": "Current active account, organization, known read/update permission, purchasing access and password assurance are required for writes/replays. Scope and cross-object attempts denied. Drafts do not retain passwords or bearer links; scope changes clear credentials and discard late results.",
    "frontend_design_system": "Existing dashboard token scope restored without shell duplication. Product brand-action token used for the primary button. Draft/selection remain distinct from recorded results. Frozen item names replace technical line IDs.",
    "workflow_accessibility_localization": "EN/FR workbench, errors and protected-route guidance; exact string quantity localization; explicit confirmation; keyboard entry/receipt focus; recoverable drafts. 320/390/768/1440 layouts and 200% CSS text verified. Native AT/zoom and wider shell localization remain open.",
    "product_operations": "Buyer can prepare a private invitation, inspect supplier consequences, record a reasoned decision and disable access. Current and earlier records support reconciliation. Creating a link does not send it.",
    "finance_reconciliation_controls": "Original PO quantities/totals/approval and financial records unchanged by acknowledgement operations. Buyer acceptance cannot receive stock, authorize payment or alter AP/ledger. Downstream controlled operations remain separate.",
    "statutory_country": "Not applicable to calculation changes: no statutory/country-pack/tax/posting rule changed. No OHADA/SYSCOHADA approval or certification is asserted.",
    "audit_records": "Durable actor/request/correlation and state/event/audit references support exact recovery and retention. Revocation does not erase history. Partial historical content-integrity limitation is explicit.",
    "quality_release": "102 tests in 14 distinct suites after correction of one test harness import; nine owned PostgreSQL groups; two authenticated EN/FR browser journeys; 24 screenshots and ten layout cases; final typecheck and fifteen-file lint.",
    "sre_performance_cost": "Reads bounded to five envelopes and ten invitations/proposals per envelope with scoped cursors. Measured development readiness only; no approved production budget claim. No new worker or provider cost.",
    "purchasing_ap": "Buyer/supplier/buyer handoff verified against existing acknowledgement domain. Supplier identity, commercial assent, PO approval and operational amendments are not inferred from a bearer response.",
    "saas_packaging": "Existing purchasing entitlement reused. Explicit empty/read-only/expired/suspended grants tested. No package pricing, billing provider or commercial activation added.",
    "api_events": "No new public route. Existing supplier API exercised; current actions use existing applied events and mandatory audit. No external event/provider delivery.",
    "rollout_support": "Ship matching contracts, services, actions, UI and messages together; retain immutable records and exact pending requests on rollback. Operator guide names required inputs and their sources.",
